                <pb facs="0160" n="56" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg56"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.4515 Air Pollution/414: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Canada
                        (Boal)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-03-07T18:00:00-05:00">March 7, 1933—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9. Your telegram No. 7, March 1, 4 p.m. Express to Department of External Affairs
                    appreciation of Canadian Government’s willingness to enter upon negotiations and
                    inquire when Canadian representative will be prepared to open discussion.
                    Qualification referred to in Canadian note may be discussed in course of
                    negotiations along with other questions which will arise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
